---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro"
import CheckPanel from "../components/CheckPanel.astro"
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "")
const REPO = "https://github.com/andrew1234-arch/Mene"
---
<Base title="Mene">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="triad">MENE · TEKEL · UPHARSIN</p>
      <h1>The writing on the wall for poisoned packages.</h1>
      <p class="lede">On 8 September 2025 one phished maintainer turned chalk and debug into malware. The warnings lived where they could be edited or deleted. Mene writes them where they can't be.</p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="btn primary" href={`${base}/wall`}>Read the wall</a>
        <a class="btn" href={`${base}/check`}>Check your lockfile</a>
        <a class="btn" href={`${REPO}#github-action`}>Add to CI</a>
      </div>
      <dl class="counters" aria-live="polite">
        <div><dt>Active advisories</dt><dd id="c-active">…</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Witnesses</dt><dd id="c-witnesses">…</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Last inscription</dt><dd id="c-block" class="mono">…</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <CheckPanel />
  </section>

  <section class="grid3 panels">
    <article class="card">
      <p class="word">Mene — numbered</p>
      <p>Every advisory is written to Arkiv and counted. It is a readonly entity, sealed to the burn address in the same transaction, so not even its author can delete it. <a href={`${REPO}#trust-model`}>How</a></p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <p class="word">Tekel — weighed</p>
      <p>Independent witnesses weigh it, and 2 of 3 must confirm. Mene counts a confirmation by the wallet that signed it, so one hacked witness can neither forge a warning nor bury one. <a href={`${REPO}#trust-model`}>Why</a></p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <p class="word">Upharsin — divided</p>
      <p>The poisoned version is cut from your build. Your lockfile is matched on your machine, and CI fails until you install the safe version. <a href={`${REPO}#github-action`}>Setup</a></p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <h2>How a warning becomes binding</h2>
  <figure class="card diagram">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 760 210" role="img" aria-labelledby="qd-t">
      <title id="qd-t">Witness A inscribes an advisory; witness B confirms; with 2 of 3 witnesses confirming, the advisory is ACTIVE and CI fails on a match.</title>
      <g font-family="var(--sans)" font-size="14" fill="var(--text)">
        <rect x="10" y="20" width="150" height="44" rx="8" fill="var(--bg-2)" stroke="var(--line)"/><text x="85" y="47" text-anchor="middle">Witness A inscribes</text>
        <rect x="10" y="83" width="150" height="44" rx="8" fill="var(--bg-2)" stroke="var(--line)"/><text x="85" y="110" text-anchor="middle">Witness B confirms</text>
        <rect x="10" y="146" width="150" height="44" rx="8" fill="var(--bg-2)" stroke="var(--line)" stroke-dasharray="4 4"/><text x="85" y="173" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)">Witness C (optional)</text>
        <path d="M160 42 C 230 42, 230 105, 290 105 M160 105 L290 105 M160 168 C 230 168, 230 105, 290 105" stroke="var(--gold)" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5"/>
        <rect x="290" y="72" width="180" height="66" rx="10" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--gold)"/>
        <text x="380" y="100" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--serif)" font-size="22" fill="var(--gold)">Arkiv</text>
        <text x="380" y="122" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="var(--muted)">2 of 3 confirmations</text>
        <path d="M470 105 L560 105" stroke="var(--gold)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#arr)"/>
        <rect x="560" y="72" width="190" height="66" rx="10" fill="var(--gold)"/>
        <text x="655" y="100" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600" fill="var(--gold-ink)">ACTIVE</text>
        <text x="655" y="122" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="var(--gold-ink)">your CI fails on a match</text>
      </g>
      <defs><marker id="arr" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" fill="var(--gold)"/></marker></defs>
    </svg>
  </figure>

  <h2>Thirty seconds to a safer build</h2>
  <div class="two">
    <div>
      <p class="muted small">From the command line</p>
<pre><code>git clone {REPO} && cd Mene
npm ci && npm run build
node packages/cli/dist/index.js check --lockfile ../app/package-lock.json
# exit 0 clean · 1 poisoned · 2 can't verify (fails closed)</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="muted small">In GitHub Actions</p>
<pre><code>- uses: andrew1234-arch/Mene/action@main
  with:
    lockfile: package-lock.json</code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="story">
    <h2>The writing on the wall</h2>
    <p>In the book of Daniel, chapter 5, King Belshazzar holds a feast. A hand appears and writes four words on the palace wall, opposite the lampstand: <em>Mene, Mene, Tekel, Upharsin</em>. Numbered, weighed, divided. Nobody at the feast can wipe them away.</p>
    <p>A supply-chain warning should work the same way. Everyone can read it, and nobody can quietly erase it.</p>
  </section>

  <h2 id="threats">What an attacker can and can't do</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Attacker</th><th>Tries to</th><th>What happens</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Anyone</td><td>Publish a fake advisory with Mene's labels</td><td>It never appears. Every read is pinned to the witnesses' wallets with <code>createdBy()</code>, and an entity's creator can't be changed.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>One stolen witness key</td><td>Force a false warning</td><td>It stays <em>PENDING 1/2</em>. It needs a second witness.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>One stolen witness key</td><td>Withdraw a real warning</td><td>One withdrawal isn't a quorum. The advisory stays ACTIVE.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>The advisory's author</td><td>Edit or delete it</td><td>It can't be edited: it's readonly. Deletion fails: it's sealed to the burn address.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>A witness</td><td>Delete their own confirmation</td><td>Every client that saw it keeps counting it, and the Wall raises a deletion alarm.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Mene's authors</td><td>Take the site down</td><td>There's no server. The CLI and any copy of this site read Arkiv directly.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Time</td><td>Let advisories expire</td><td>Any wallet can pay for a Lifetime Extension with <code>mene keepalive</code>. No permission needed.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p class="small"><a href={`${REPO}#threat-model`}>Threat model and limitations in the README →</a></p>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 1fr; gap: 3rem; align-items: center; padding: 3.5rem 0 2rem; }
  .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 3.9rem); text-wrap: balance; }
  .lede { font-size: 1.12rem; color: var(--muted); max-width: 54ch; }
  .cta { display: flex; gap: .6rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 1.5rem 0 1.8rem; }
  .counters { display: flex; gap: 2.2rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 0; }
  .counters dt { color: var(--muted); font-size: .78rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; }
  .counters dd { margin: 0; font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 2.1rem; color: var(--gold); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .counters dd.mono { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 1.15rem; padding-top: .65rem; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; padding-top: 2rem; } }
  .panels { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .word { font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; color: var(--gold); font-size: 1.45rem; margin: 0 0 .4rem; }
  .diagram svg { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
  .two { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; }
  .two > div { min-width: 0; }
  .story { max-width: 68ch; }
  .story p { font-size: 1.05rem; }
</style>

<script>
  import { getTrust, watchWall } from "../scripts/mene"
  const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id)!
  $("c-witnesses").textContent = String(getTrust().issuers.length)
  watchWall(
    (w) => {
      $("c-active").textContent = String(w.statuses.filter((s) => s.status === "ACTIVE").length)
      const last = Math.max(0, ...w.statuses.map((s) => s.advisory?.createdAt ?? 0))
      $("c-block").textContent = last ? `#${last}` : "—"
    },
    () => {
      $("c-active").textContent = "—"
      $("c-block").textContent = "—"
    },
  )
</script>
